You can use `Password.TryAgain` with a `StringComparison` of `Ordinary`. It takes an integer `n` that represents the maximum number of times you want to guess. For 10 tries, `n` should be 10. The method returns a boolean indicating success or failure.

```java
String password = "foobar";
int tries = 10;

try {
    String input = Password.TryAgain(password, StringComparison.Ordinal);
    if (!password.getPassword()) {
        System.out.println("Failed");
        return false;
    }
} catch (Exception e) {
    System.err. println("Failed");
}
```

